1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:09,450
Sideways pixels, plus a note: turn 90.

2
00:00:09,450 --> 00:00:15,770
Does FFmpeg follow the note?

3
00:00:15,770 --> 00:00:25,290
Stored 320x180. Tag: rotate 90.

4
00:00:25,290 --> 00:00:38,610
Two readers: ffprobe, and a decoded comparison.

5
00:00:38,610 --> 00:00:43,950
Re-encode: 180x320, no tag, upright.

6
00:00:43,950 --> 00:00:51,420
-c copy: sideways pixels plus tag, upright.

7
00:00:51,420 --> 00:01:00,830
-vf transpose=1 on top of autorotate.

8
00:01:00,830 --> 00:01:08,680
Result: no tag, sideways again.

9
00:01:08,680 --> 00:01:15,870
-noautorotate: 6.1.1 keeps the tag.

10
00:01:15,870 --> 00:01:23,060
8.1.2 drops it: plays sideways.

11
00:01:23,060 --> 00:01:33,530
By hand on 6.1.1: tag kept, upside down.

12
00:01:33,530 --> 00:01:42,690
By hand on 8.1.2: tag dropped, upright.

13
00:01:42,690 --> 00:01:49,000
Let FFmpeg turn it. No transpose on top.

14
00:01:49,000 --> 00:01:54,520
Not tested: phone files, other angles, players.
